B.b_O=new A.du("scoreOverlap",'Rank a catalogue against a live selection by SET OVERLAP and write the survivors into a results table. Each catalogue row carries a list of ids in `listColumn` (JSON array or a comma/semicolon/pipe string) and optionally a weaker set in `secondaryColumn`; the pick lives in `selectionTable`.`selectionColumn` (e.g. the `anatomy` node\'s `selectionTable` mirror). Every row sharing at least one id is copied into `into` with its coverage stamped on \u2014 hits, secondary hits, extras (ids beyond the pick), the matched names, an "n/m" summary and ONE descending `rank`, so the results screen is a plain sorted list. `mode` picks what rank means: "coverage" (most of your pick first) or "focus" (fewest extras first). An empty selection empties `into`.',B.bui,"data",!1)
