B.cTv=new A.p("density",B.bD,'Card treatment density. "card" (default) is the classic multi-line card; "row" renders a compact single-line tile (~44-52px): leading checkbox/dot/icon, title, up to 2 trailing tag chips, whole-row tap.',B.bvH,null)
B.d2m=new A.p("sectionLabel",B.D,"An eyebrow header owned by this node, rendered ABOVE its cards \u2014 but ONLY while the list actually has rows right now (reactive: reads the same live row set the node already recomputes). Lets a category caption disappear along with its list instead of sitting over an empty panel (design-real-estate-efficiency \u2014 wikipick-0830ui); may be a {lang: text} map.",B.f,null)
B.cWO=new A.p("combineEmptyAlsoEmptyTable",B.at,"Opt-in gate so two sibling `cards` nodes on one screen can share ONE combined empty panel instead of each showing its own: this node's authored empty* props render ONLY when this table is empty AND the named sibling table is ALSO currently empty; when the sibling still has rows, this node renders nothing at all (design-real-estate-efficiency \u2014 wikipick-0830ui).",B.f,null)
B.cVj=new A.p("dotColumn",B.t,"Column whose value maps (via `colors`) to a small leading color dot \u2014 works in both `density` modes. Falls back to `imageColumn`/`iconColumn` when those are also set (dot is the lowest-priority leading affordance).",B.f,null)
B.cVt=new A.p("toggle",B.V,"Row density only: show a tappable checkbox as the leading affordance instead of the image/icon/dot, wired to `statusColumn`/`doneValue`/`openValue` (same toggleField convention agenda/tree/list use).",B.f,null)
