B.cUR=new A.p("scopeRowId",B.D,"OPT-IN subtree scope (rehome-0804, mirrors `priolanes`' `scopeRowId`): a literal row id or a `$`-token (`$rowId`, `$selected:<table>`). Unconfigured (absent) leaves the card population byte-identical. Configured but UNRESOLVED (e.g. a `$selected:` token with nothing selected) fails CLOSED to the empty set \u2014 never falls back to the whole board. Configured + resolved keeps only rows reachable walking `scopeEdgesTable` DOWNWARD (contains edges) from the resolved row id; the root row itself is included.",B.f,null)
B.EF=new A.p("scopeEdgesTable",B.at,'With `scopeRowId`: the edges table to walk (default "relations").',B.f,null)
B.d1y=new A.p("scopeEdgeFrom",B.t,'With `scopeRowId`: the edge\'s parent-id column (default "from" \u2014 matches `priolanes`\' own default; set explicitly when the edges table uses different column names, e.g. "fromId").',B.f,null)
B.EB=new A.p("scopeEdgeTo",B.t,'With `scopeRowId`: the edge\'s child-id column (default "to").',B.f,null)
B.EH=new A.p("scopeEdgeType",B.t,'With `scopeRowId`: the edge-kind column checked against `scopeContainsType` (default "type").',B.f,null)
B.EJ=new A.p("scopeContainsType",B.D,'With `scopeRowId`: the edge-kind value meaning "contains" (default "contains").',B.f,null)
B.d1u=new A.p("limit",B.ag,'dispusab-0804: opt-in TOP-N cap \u2014 render at most N cards, applied AFTER scope, filter, live search/column filters and sort, so `limit: 3` means "the top 3 of what this view would have shown". The PREVIEW idiom: a compact strip on an overview screen beside a button that opens the full view. Unset / <= 0 renders every row (byte-identical to before); a limit larger than the row count is a no-op.',B.f,null)
