B.cUH=new A.p("onLinkTap",B.X,'Action spec { fn, args } fired when a Markdown `[label](target)` link is tapped; `"$value"` in args is replaced by the raw link target, unmodified \u2014 the same contract `notepad`\'s `onLinkTap` uses. Unset \u2192 links render styled but inert.',B.f,null)
B.d6P=new A.p("jumpToSectionSetting",B.D,'Board-settings key whose value `"<nonce>::<heading text>"` scrolls to the first matching `#`/`##`/`###` heading (trimmed, case-insensitive). The leading nonce lets a repeated tap on the same section re-trigger. The landing position is an ESTIMATE \u2014 "near this section", not frame-perfect.',B.f,null)
B.d0O=new A.p("findEnabledSetting",B.D,'Opt-in "Find in article" \u2014 restores the same feature `notepad`\'s `findEnabledSetting` offers, dropped when this applet migrated from `notepad` to `bookreader`. Names a board-settings key an external affordance (e.g. a summoned action-footer\'s find icon) toggles true/false to open/close an inline search bar docked above the page. The typed query, per-occurrence match highlighting, match-count feedback ("N of M"), next/prev stepping and scroll-to-match are all self-contained in this widget \u2014 no other prop or host wiring is needed. Unset (default) \u2192 zero footprint, byte-identical to before this prop existed.',B.f,null)
