B.cYV=new A.p("prioColumn",B.t,'Priority quick-set (priolanes2-0726): same idiom as statusColumn \u2014 a row\'s \u22ee menu offers "Priority: <value>" per prioOptions entry (plus a Clear item once set), writing it to this column (one undo step). Engine-generic; Dispatch wires it to `prioLane`.',B.f,null)
B.cU1=new A.p("prioOptions",B.X,"List of priority values offered by the prioColumn quick-set menu.",B.f,null)
B.cSr=new A.p("prioLabels",B.X,"Optional {value: label} display overrides for prioOptions entries; unset values show their raw string.",B.f,null)
B.cMV=new A.p("recursive",B.V,'An item can have BOTH its own detail AND children (no folder/file split) \u2014 every selected item shows its detail, any item with children is expandable, and "New <item>"/addItems add a child of the selected item.',B.f,null)
B.cPX=new A.p("ownerColumn",B.t,"When set AND a rowId is injected (this explorer is itself a master-detail DETAIL child), the list filters to rows whose value in this column equals that injected id, and new rows are stamped with it.",B.f,null)
B.d4S=new A.p("detailedView",B.V,"Two-level rail: column 2 (contents) offers a Directory \u27f7 Detailed toggle in its header \u2014 compact rows vs. a per-row progress DASHBOARD (status chip, progress bar, subtask/log-entry counts, the existing `tags` chips for priority/importance/due/assignee, and a one-line latest-activity preview), plus a compact done/active/queued rollup summary + bar at the top of the column for the open folder. Reads the existing showProgress rollup cache; never a second board walk.",B.f,null)
B.bwe=s(["directory","detailed"],t.s)
B.cT7=new A.p("defaultContentsView",B.bD,'detailedView: initial column-2 toggle state. Unset \u2192 "directory" (unchanged compact rows on first open).',B.bwe,null)
B.cOv=new A.p("projectOverview",B.V,"Opt-in PER-PROJECT overview dashboard \u2014 a third Tasks \u21c4 Overview segment in column 2's (contents) header, alongside the existing detailedView Directory/Detailed toggle. Off by default so no existing applet's UI changes. When on, selecting a project can switch its contents column to a computed bar/pie breakdown of every item in that project's contains-subtree. See overviewTagsColumn/overviewTypeColumn for the two breakdown columns.",B.f,null)
B.d1K=new A.p("valueLabels",B.X,"Opt-in raw-value \u2192 display map for rendered DATA VALUES (tree row status/tag chips, the projectOverview by-status/by-tag/by-type chart bucket labels): {raw: text-or-{lang:text}} or column-keyed {column: {raw: ...}}, resolved against the ambient locale; unmapped values render exactly as before (passthrough, never blank). Display-only \u2014 stored values, filter payloads and tag `colors` keys stay RAW.",B.f,null)
B.cZu=new A.p("overviewTagsColumn",B.t,"projectOverview: the multi-value (List<String>) column the overview's \"by tag\" bar chart buckets on \u2014 each item can carry more than one tag, so every tag it holds counts once in that tag's bucket (a scalar column works too; each row then counts once under its own value). Unset hides the tag breakdown.",B.f,null)
B.d4A=new A.p("overviewTypeColumn",B.t,'projectOverview: the scalar column the overview\'s "by type" bar chart buckets on (e.g. group/task/note/goal/milestone/...). Unset hides that breakdown.',B.f,null)
B.d3L=new A.p("overviewMarkerColumns",B.jy,"projectOverview: boolean columns (e.g. bottleneck/blocked) whose true value marks an item as needing attention in the overview's \"Needs attention\" section \u2014 one group per configured column, titled by that column's own schema label. Empty (default) adds no marker groups; the no-responsible-person and stale groups are always generic and still show.",B.f,null)
B.cVK=new A.p("overviewDueColumn",B.t,"projectOverview: the date column read for the overview's Overdue needs-attention group. Unset skips the Overdue group entirely.",B.f,null)
B.d_t=new A.p("overviewLogColumn",B.t,"projdash-0810 fix-forward: boolean column marking a descendant as LOG CHATTER (an entrythread comment/reply) rather than a first-class project item \u2014 the SAME column an entrythread node's own opt-in `logEntryColumn` stamps true on every composed entry. When set, projectOverview's item population (`_overviewDescendants`) excludes flagged rows from the headline count, the status/tag/type breakdowns and the item list \u2014 a task with 300 log comments no longer inflates \"items total\" or the active-status pie. Unset (default) is a no-op: nothing is excluded, matching pre-fix behavior. Attachment-kind children (`leafAttachmentKinds`) are excluded unconditionally, no config needed.",B.f,null)
B.d2D=new A.p("activeStatus",B.D,'detailedView: statusColumn value counted as "active" in the active/queued split (default "active").',B.f,null)
B.cSI=new A.p("queuedStatus",B.D,'detailedView: statusColumn value counted as "queued" (default "queued").',B.f,null)
B.cXJ=new A.p("activityColumn",B.t,'detailedView: column holding the text shown as a row\'s one-line latest-activity/comment preview (default "comment").',B.f,null)
B.cY2=new A.p("activityTimeColumn",B.t,'detailedView: column used to find the most recent child/descendant for the latest-activity preview (default "postedAt"); must resolve to a parseable date/dateTime column.',B.f,null)
B.cQR=new A.p("alwaysShowDetail",B.V,'Two-level, wide layout: when a project (folder) is selected/opened and no child ends up auto-selected, show the project\'s OWN detail (requires `recursive`) instead of the "pick a task" placeholder.',B.f,null)
B.cXo=new A.p("detailKindLabel",B.V,'Show a small "Project"/"Task" header label above the detail pane\'s content \u2014 nouns derived from newFolderLabel/newFileLabel (strip a leading "New "), override via folderNoun/fileNoun.',B.f,null)
B.cX8=new A.p("folderNoun",B.D,'detailKindLabel override: the noun shown for a folder ("Project"). May be a {lang: text} map.',B.f,null)
B.cRO=new A.p("fileNoun",B.D,'detailKindLabel override: the noun shown for a leaf ("Task"). May be a {lang: text} map.',B.f,null)
B.cRz=new A.p("settingsAction",B.X,"Opt-in: {fn, args?, label?} \u2014 a gear affordance shown next to a selected FOLDER's detail header, fired with that row's id (like menuActions, but a single, separate surface for FEATURE settings \u2014 e.g. sharing/members \u2014 kept distinct from the row \u22ee menu's quick actions and from the attributes/edit-details form's data fields).",B.f,null)
B.cRp=new A.p("rootDashboard",B.V,'Two-level rail: the synthetic root ("Projects", nothing selected) gets a COMPUTED cross-project progress dashboard as its detail \u2014 overall done/active/queued rollup plus one row per top-level project \u2014 built from the existing showProgress rollup cache. The root stays synthetic: no new record, no reparenting.',B.f,null)
B.d5C=new A.p("filterable",B.V,"Opt-in per-column filtering of the TASKS/children column (the two-level rail's column 2, and the narrow children-directory list) via the unified Add-filter engine \u2014 mirrors agenda/tree/cards/report's own \"filterable\" opt-in (AddFilterBar<Record> + applyColFilters). Off (default) renders exactly as before. Session-scoped state only; the pinned strip and the projects (column-1/root) list are never filtered.",B.f,null)
B.cUk=new A.p("followSelection",B.V,"Two-way sync with `board.settings['sel:<table>']`: an external write (e.g. a notepad's resolved [[Wiki Link]] tap) selects + reveals that row here; picking a row here publishes back to the same setting. Off by default (no behavior change).",B.f,null)
B.cPF=new A.p("id",B.D,"This node's handle \u2014 required for the explorerSetPanelVisible runtime action (and panelChannel) to target it (an id-less explorer still renders, just not runtime-controllable).",B.f,null)
B.cMo=new A.p("panelChannel",B.V,"Opt-in (roundb-0720-eng): the three rail panels (tree/contents/detail) collapse state is read/written through BoardState.effectiveExplorerPanelVisible/setExplorerPanelVisible (runtime-overridable via the explorerSetPanelVisible action) instead of pure session-local widget state. Requires this node's `id`. Off (default): byte-identical to today, pure private State.",B.f,null)
B.cOW=new A.p("twoLevel",B.V,"Two-column rail: column 1 lists top-level folders/projects, column 2 the selected one's children, before the detail view.",B.f,null)
B.cPk=new A.p("autoSelectFirstChild",B.V,"On selecting a folder, immediately select its first child so the detail pane is never empty.",B.f,null)
B.d6H=new A.p("colorColumn",B.t,"Optional per-row colour column (ramp name or #hex) tinting the rail entry.",B.f,null)
B.cSQ=new A.p("emojiColumn",B.t,"Optional column holding a leading emoji shown on each rail entry.",B.f,null)
B.d00=new A.p("cardRows",B.V,"Render each rail row as a rounded card surface (margin + border) instead of a flat list row, so an items panel reads as pretty cards.",B.f,null)
B.d5Y=new A.p("clearSelectionOnBackgroundTap",B.V,'With followSelection on, tapping empty rail background clears the current sel:<table> selection (same as the "Scoped to: X \u2715" chip). On by default when followSelection is set; set false to opt a followSelection explorer out.',B.f,null)
B.d_k=new A.p("newValues",B.X,'Values stamped on every new leaf (New <file> and addItems), token-resolved like a composer write (e.g. {"createdBy": "$playerId"}); addItems\' own "values" override these per-item.',B.f,null)
B.bDX=s([B.cUB,B.d6i,B.cOR,B.d6C,B.cWV,B.d22,B.cXb,B.d_b,B.d6L,B.d2G,B.cVa,B.cSE,B.d1i,B.cZz,B.cXs,B.cVT,B.cVh,B.cYQ,B.d4b,B.cYN,B.d3o,B.cTx,B.d1N,B.cUd,B.cYv,B.cXF,B.d_Z,B.cSd,B.d57,B.cZD,B.cPG,B.d32,B.d4d,B.cZa,B.cMU,B.cSj,B.cNz,B.cZ6,B.cYa,B.cUx,B.d1b,B.d6r,B.d5V,B.d5J,B.cVd,B.cOt,B.cQX,B.cQW,B.d4Q,B.cU4,B.cZq,B.cWh,B.cSi,B.d35,B.d63,B.cWI,B.d6X,B.d61,B.cMC,B.cZf,B.cYX,B.cU_,B.d1M,B.d2L,B.d6y,B.cVr,B.cTq,B.d3f,B.d0z,B.d0x,B.cZk,B.cVL,B.cWS,B.d06,B.d0f,B.cWk,B.cXR,B.cWH,B.cOO,B.d__,B.cYV,B.cU1,B.cSr,B.cMV,B.cPX,B.d4S,B.cT7,B.cOv,B.d1K,B.cZu,B.d4A,B.d3L,B.cVK,B.d_t,B.d2D,B.cSI,B.cXJ,B.cY2,B.cQR,B.cXo,B.cX8,B.cRO,B.cRz,B.cRp,B.d5C,B.cUk,B.cPF,B.cMo,B.cOW,B.cPk,B.d6H,B.cSQ,B.d00,B.d5Y,B.d_k,B.EC],t.G)
B.cBT=new A.d1("explorer","Master-detail file browser: a collapsible left folder-tree (nested via a self-referential parent column) drives a configurable detail view of the selected file. New/rename/delete (recoverable Trash) on the rail.",B.bDX,!1)
B.cVX=new A.p("table",B.at,'Files table (default "files").',B.f,null)
B.cWF=new A.p("fileId",B.D,'The open file\'s id; usually injected as "rowId" by an explorer detail.',B.f,null)
B.cRT=new A.p("parentColumn",B.t,'Self-referential parent id linking pages to their file (default "parentId").',B.f,null)
B.cRg=new A.p("nameColumn",B.t,'Page-name column (default "name").',B.f,null)
B.d1j=new A.p("orderColumn",B.t,'Order column for pages (default "order").',B.f,null)
B.cZV=new A.p("kindColumn",B.t,'Column marking a row as a page (default "kind").',B.f,null)
B.cW_=new A.p("pageValue",B.D,'kindColumn value that means "page" (default "page").',B.f,null)
B.d_l=new A.p("pageLabel",B.D,'Noun for a page: Page / Canvas / Sheet (default "Page").',B.f,null)
B.cTO=new A.p("fileIsFirstPage",B.V,"Treat the file row itself as page 1 (default true).",B.f,null)
